A||||2||fiero56||New tires and a rant||||1||
Z||000000||fiero56||10-28-2001||01:09 AM||||Just had 4 new Yokohama Avid H4s mounted on my Formula today(BTW: Thank you 87ECO5!). It took a few miles for them to break-in, but I love them. They ride so much softer than my Pirelli did. They stick well, and are even quieter at highway speed than the Pirelli(I dind't think it was possible for tires to be quieter than those were).<P>My only complaint so far is the sidewall is a little softer than the Pirelli, so steering response is not quite as immediate with my poly.<P><BR>Decided to take them on the highway for a more extended run tonight. 20 miles each way. About 30 miles in, my SES light flicks on, and doesn't go out. 45K miles I've been driving this car, and this is the FIRST time it has ever tripped that light. Drove home the last 10 miles, varying speed trying to find symptoms. Never got it off. I will pull the code(s) tommorrow and check it out. It sounded like it was running rich, and the inside of the tips is filthy black(weren't before). So, I've got some playing to do tommorrow.<P>BTW: I love my H4s.<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pffsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||10-28-2001||02:46 AM||||Yup, the H4's rule.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Got a pair on the front with Yoko S305's on the back.  Love 'em.<P>If it sounded like it was running rich, your o2 sensor might have given up the ghost.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||10-28-2001||10:56 AM||||Pulled code 32 from the computer. EGR valve held a vacuum, all lines looked good. Turned out a rubber elbow wasn't sealing tight enough off the plenum. 1 zip-tie later, and no more codes.||||reg||1
